.TH TUIWEATHERGIRL 1 "23 September 2026" "1.5.12" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tuiweathergirl \- A terminal weather and disaster monitoring station
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuiweathergirl
[\0\fIoptions\fR\0]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBtuiweathergirl\fR is a terminal-based weather and disaster monitoring station. It supports real-time monitoring of weather, polar research stations, atmospheric conditions across multiple global locations, and space weather.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show summary of options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-ver ", " \-\-version
Print application version.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-updateapp
Check for updates, download, and install them. Note: This self-update mechanism is intended only for standalone installations cloned from GitHub. System packages installed via a package manager should be updated through your distribution repository (e.g., \fBapt update && apt upgrade\fR).
.TP
\fB\-au\fR [\fIon\fR|\fIoff\fR], \fB\-\-autoupdateapp\fR [\fIon\fR|\fIoff\fR]
Enable or disable auto-updates (\fBon\fR/\fBoff\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-view\fR \fIVIEWNAME\fR
Select the application view (\fBsetup\fR, \fBbasic\fR, \fBmotivate\fR, \fBdashboard\fR, \fBttydashboard\fR, \fBseasonal\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fITHEMENAME\fR
Select the color scheme (\fBmain\fR, \fBmono\fR, \fBlemon\fR, \fBarctic\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-addcity\fR \fICITYNAME\fR
Add a new city to follow by city name. Must be used with \fB\-\-country\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-removecity\fR \fICITYNUMBER\fR
Remove a currently followed city by its index number.
.TP
\fB\-\-sethome\fR \fICITYNUMBER\fR
Set the home city index (city must already be added).
.TP
\fB\-\-country\fR \fICOUNTRYNAME\fR
Specify the country name for \fB\-\-addcity\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable verbose debug output on errors.
.TP
.BR \-clr ", " \-\-clearcache
Clear application cache, application log, and warnings log.
.TP
\fB\-reqt\fR \fISECONDSNUMBER\fR, \fB\-\-requesttimeout\fR \fISECONDSNUMBER\fR
Set the HTTP request timeout in seconds (default: 5).
.TP
.BR \-ls ", " \-\-listfiles
List paths to application log files, configuration, and runtime data.
.TP
.BR \-lsps ", " \-\-listpolarstations
List all followable Antarctic and Arctic Polar Stations.
.TP
\fB\-lat\fR \fILATFLOAT\fR, \fB\-\-latitude\fR \fILATFLOAT\fR
Specify geographical latitude. Use Google Maps or a GPS to obtain it.
.TP
\fB\-lon\fR \fILONFLOAT\fR, \fB\-\-longitude\fR \fILONFLOAT\fR
Specify geographical longitude. Use Google Maps or a GPS to obtain it.
.TP
\fB\-csort\fR \fIORDER\fR, \fB\-\-citiessorting\fR \fIORDER\fR
Select city sorting order (\fBunsorted\fR, \fBcity\fR, \fBcountry\fR). If chosen \fBcity\fR or \fBcountry\fR, any city from the home country would be sorted at the top.
.TP
.B \-\-updatepolicy
Print the application update policy.

.SH VIEWS
.TP
\fBmotivate\fR, \fBbasic\fR
Best for lightweight terminals or pure virtual TTY consoles (simple STDOUT).
.TP
.B ttydashboard
A colorful ncurses dashboard designed for virtual consoles (requires at least 106x33 terminal geometry).
.TP
.B dashboard
The main interactive dashboard featuring full metrics (requires at least 146x38 terminal geometry).
.TP
.B setup
Prints currently configured cities.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NASAFIRMSAPIKEY
Optional API key for displaying detailed wildfire data. Request a free key at:
\fIhttps://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key\fR

.SH NOTES
If \fBtuiweathergirl\fR was installed via a system package manager (e.g., \fBdpkg\fR or \fBapt\fR), do not use the built-in \fB\-\-updateapp\fR feature. System installations should be updated exclusively through your system's package management tools to preserve filesystem integrity.

For details on how to use this application, please visit the project GitHub home where you will find a detailed documentation illustrated with screenshots and tutorial videos. The URL is at the bottom of this man page.

.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
If the config file was manually edited and the application starts throwing exceptions as a result, just delete the config file and run the application again - it will re-create the config from scratch.

For more troubleshooting details, please read the official documentation on the project GitHub page.

.SH BUGS
No known bugs. Report bugs to the upstream project page.

